   "verbatim": {
    "text": "Site 1 is situated almost in the centre of the Strand, and is the closest inshore. The site is represented by a distinct pattern of magnetometer readings covering an area 165 by 40 m, suggesting a wide scatter of ferrous remains (Fig. 1c). Due to its exposed position the site is the most dynamic of the three. Its depth varies between 3.8 and 5.2 m depending on the state of the tide and sand accretion (all depths are mean averages for the centres of the sites as indicated by magnetometer readings). Sand overburden has reached a maximum measured depth of 0.8 m above the highest known part of the wreck and at its lowest point is 1.2 m below the same point, represented by a wrought iron anchor.",
    "locator": "Birch & McElvogue 1999 p. 270",
    "observer_role": "reporter"
   },
   "label_by_authors": "La Juliana",
   "attributions": [
    {
