   "verbatim": {
    "text": "Site 3. 20 m south-west from Site 2 is the largest group of readings, covering some 270 m by 72 m. The depth of water recorded on the site varies between 3.8 and 5.0 m depending on the state of the tide and the sand overburden. Monitoring of the sites indicates that Site 3 is where the maximum sand accretion occurs; this being influenced by Streedagh Point which acts as barrier to south-west wind generated swell.",
    "locator": "Birch & McElvogue 1999 p. 271",
